# Mars Rover Kata - Project Structure

This is a Ruby implementation of the Mars Rover Kata, following a clean object-oriented design.

## Core Components

The main implementation files are located in the `lib` directory:

- [mars_rover.rb](mdc:lib/mars_rover.rb) - The main Mars Rover class that handles rover movement and commands
- [orientation.rb](mdc:lib/orientation.rb) - Manages the rover's orientation (North, South, East, West)
- [position.rb](mdc:lib/position.rb) - Handles the rover's position coordinates on the grid

## Tests

The test suite is in the `spec` directory:

- [mars_rover_commands_spec.rb](mdc:spec/mars_rover_commands_spec.rb) - Tests for rover movement commands
- [mars_rover_initializing_spec.rb](mdc:spec/mars_rover_initializing_spec.rb) - Tests for rover initialization
- [spec_helper.rb](mdc:spec/spec_helper.rb) - RSpec configuration and test helpers

## Development

The project uses:
- RSpec for testing
- [Gemfile](mdc:Gemfile) for dependency management
- [tcr.sh](mdc:tcr.sh) for test && commit || revert workflow
